  "items": [
    {
      "LF_sha256": "a08fe621d562abe2f2a9a8dc318d35bb7caf56fa3b2d1fce356043a8d7c377c7",
      "RAW_bytes": 645,
      "RAW_range": [
        250262,
        250907
      ],
      "RAW_sha256": "a08fe621d562abe2f2a9a8dc318d35bb7caf56fa3b2d1fce356043a8d7c377c7",
      "classification": "EXCLUDED",
      "clipped_at_region_boundary": true,
      "formula": null,
      "item_id": "S001",
      "kind": "source_block",
      "nodes": [],
      "reason": "Earlier full-gradient generator discussion; selected rate uses actual residual gradient.",
      "region_id": "algorithm-and-prop31",
      "source_URL": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#S3.SS2.p3.2",
      "source_id": "S3.SS2.p3.2",
      "source_tag": "p",
      "text": "The first line is the Hamiltonian flow associated with the quadratic coupling potential: between bounces, it rotates $(x-y)/\\sqrt{\\eta}$ and $p$ . This use of a quadratic reference flow, with the remaining force handled by bounce events, is analogous to the Boomerang sampler [ 4 ] . The direct harmonic generator ( 3.3 ) still bounces against the full gradient $\\nabla V$ , so its bounce rate can remain large.",
      "independent_review": "Accepted exact source-range classification within this bounded selected universe; implementation coverage follows its named node dispositions, not automatic theorem completion."
    },
